# Public paths manifest — what migrates to the public openara-ai mirror.
#
# One pattern per line. `**` matches recursively, `*` matches a single
# path segment. Lines starting with `#` are comments. Lines starting with
# `!` exclude paths matched by an earlier pattern. Anything not matched
# stays private by default (internal/, etc.).
#
# This file is the single source of truth for the public migration script
# and for scripts/check_doc_separation.py.

# ---- Top-level public files ----
README.md
LICENSE
NOTICE
CHANGELOG.md
SECURITY.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.gitignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.public-paths
pyproject.toml
requirements.txt
requirements-api.txt
requirements-windows.txt
config.yaml

# ---- Public docs (curated; internal/docs/ stays private) ----
docs/**

# ---- Code ----
src/**
tests/**
scripts/**

# Tests for internal-only code (the file under test lives in internal/scripts/
# per CLAUDE.md "one-off migrations stay in internal/scripts/"). Mirroring
# these tests without the script they import would fail on staging/public.
!tests/test_port_faiss_to_sqlite.py

# ---- Installer / packaging assets ----
installer/**

# ---- CI and GitHub config ----
# Excluded files are meta-internal (link into internal/ or contain
# phase-specific content) and need a public-version rewrite before
# they can ship.
.github/**
!.github/copilot-instructions.md
!.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
# Workflows that are private-only:
#   - claude.yml uses an Anthropic API key
#   - build-macos-dev.yml and build-macos-full.yml are dev-only heavy CI
#   - mirror-staging.yml drives the public mirror itself; the staging deploy
#     key only exists on the private repo, so this workflow has no purpose
#     (and would always fail) if mirrored
!.github/workflows/claude.yml
!.github/workflows/build-macos-dev.yml
!.github/workflows/build-macos-full.yml
!.github/workflows/mirror-staging.yml

